Check how `process` obtains it. If it can legitimately be absent, handle that case before `validate`:
```java
if (name == null || name.isBlank()) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException("name is required");
}
```If it should never be null, the fix belongs upstream, in whatever supplies the value. `Objects.requireNonNull(name, "name")` at method entry fails earlier with a clear message.

