array.forEach with async doesnt wait. whats happening
```ts
items.forEach(async (it) => {
  await resizeImage(it);
});
console.log("done");
```

`forEach` ignores the promises returned by its callback, so it fires all of them and returns right away; "done" prints before the work finishes, and rejections become unhandled. Options:

Sequential:
```ts
for (const it of items) {
  await resizeImage(it);
}
```Parallel:
```ts
await Promise.all(items.map((it) => resizeImage(it)));
```Use `Promise.allSettled` when one failure should not stop the rest from being reported.

Hand-rolled limiter:
```ts
async function mapLimit<T, R>(xs: T[], limit: number, fn: (x: T) => Promise<R>): Promise<R[]> {
  const out: R[] = new Array(xs.length);
  let next = 0;
  const worker = async () => {
    while (next < xs.length) {
      const i = next++;
      out[i] = await fn(xs[i]);
    }
  };
  await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: limit }, worker));
  return out;
}
```Libraries like `p-limit` do the same with more features. The `next++` is safe because JavaScript is single-threaded between awaits.

